cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "qsi-extract: Extract and collate diffusion MRI scalar outputs from QSIPrep and QSIRecon into tidy longitudinal tables"
abstract: >-
  A standalone Python tool that traverses BIDS derivative trees produced by
  QSIPrep and QSIRecon, parses per-bundle and per-ROI diffusion scalar outputs
  (NODDI, DTI, tractometry), audits NODDI model-fitting assumptions, propagates
  QC flags, and writes clean longitudinal tables ready for statistical analysis.
type: software
